# harness-init .gitignore append block
#
# install.mjs picks exactly one of the two `# @profile:` sections below,
# matching the profile passed to it, and appends only that section's lines
# to the target repo's .gitignore. The `# @profile:` / `# @end` lines are
# markers for the installer, not gitignore syntax to copy verbatim.

# @profile:solo-full
# Only the relay working directory and settings.local.json are ignored;
# hook scripts and CI config are committed and reviewed like any other repo
# asset (matches HARNESSENGINEERING's own .gitignore). settings.local.json
# is per-clone Claude Code config (HYK-95: install.mjs now pre-wires it with
# absolute, machine-local paths), not a shareable repo asset like the check
# scripts -- committing it would leak this machine's local paths into a
# public repo's history.
.harness/
.claude/settings.local.json
# @end

# @profile:team-local
# The entire local harness toolchain is ignored on top of the relay
# directory — this account's personal process tooling must not be forced
# onto a shared team repo (HYK-92). Only the capture-context path is
# ignored here (not all of .claude/skills/), since a team may keep its own,
# unrelated skills under that directory that this profile has no business
# hiding (HYK-96 Scope C). settings.local.json is added for the same
# per-clone-config reason as the solo-full block above (HYK-95).
.harness/
verify.sh
hooks/commit-msg
hooks/pre-commit
scripts/check/
.claude/skills/capture-context/
.claude/settings.local.json
# @end
